:: End credits
<h1>Murdered in Plain Text</h1>
<hr class="rule">
<p style="text-align:center;">Thank you for playing.</p>

<p style="text-align:center;" class="caption">A Bits &amp; Bots production, in the tradition of File Format Fling.<br>
The PRONOM registry and the DPC Rapid Assessment Model are real, and worth your time.</p>

<div class="start-menu">
	<button class="button button--primary" data-passage="Start">Play again</button>
	<button class="button button--quiet" data-passage="Characters">The village</button>
</div>


:: Head to bed, the chamomile tea has really kicked in
You have a strange dream &mdash; or perhaps a corrupted premonition file &mdash; that someone, somewhere in the network, desperately needs your help. But the metadata is incomplete and you cannot quite resolve the identifier.

In the dream there is demonic laughter echoing along a brightly coloured village high street. The shop signs flicker like glitchy GIFs, and a peculiar figure is meticulously trimming hedges into the shape of QR codes, scanning for something. Or someone.

You jolt awake, checksum unverified. A single leaf lies on the floor beside your desk &mdash; impossible, since your home environment is strictly plant-free and climate-controlled.

Do you&hellip;

<div class="start-menu">
	<button class="button" data-passage="Try and get back to sleep">Attempt a system restore (go back to sleep)</button>
	<button class="button button--primary" data-passage="Go and investigate">Run a manual recovery (go and investigate)</button>
</div>


:: Try and get back to sleep
You sleep more deeply and silently than you ever have. No thoughts cross your mind. No packets are dropped, because none are sent.

You wake at midday to find the postman has been, with bundles of fan mail for your past work. You read the first six and give up.

<div class="start-menu">
	<button class="button" data-passage="Fan Mail Letter #1">Letter one</button>
	<button class="button" data-passage="Fan Mail Letter #2">Letter two</button>
	<button class="button" data-passage="Fan Mail Letter #3">Letter three</button>
	<button class="button" data-passage="Fan Mail Letter #4">Letter four</button>
	<button class="button" data-passage="Fan Mail Letter #5">Letter five</button>
	<button class="button" data-passage="Fan Mail Letter #6">Letter six</button>
</div>

<div class="start-menu">
	<button class="button button--quiet" data-passage="Sit back with a sigh at a job well done">Drop the rest in the bin</button>
</div>


:: Fan Mail Letter #1
<div class="letter-style">
<p>Dear Detective,</p>
<p>I am writing to thank you for solving the Riddle of the Ghost in the Cloud Storage. My aunt's holiday photographs were returned to us in full, and only slightly haunted.</p>
<p>Yours, a grateful nephew</p>
<p><em>P.S. She has since deleted them all to make room for more.</em></p>
</div>
<div class="start-menu"><<return "Next letter">></div>


:: Fan Mail Letter #2
<div class="comic-sans-letter">
<p>HELLO DETECTIVE!!!</p>
<p>I have attached a photograph of my cat, compressed to 3KB so it would fit in the envelope. Please enjoy the four remaining pixels. The orange one is his face.</p>
<p>Your biggest fan (44.1 kHz)</p>
</div>
<div class="start-menu"><<return "Next letter">></div>


:: Fan Mail Letter #3
<div class="letter-style">
<p>Sir or Madam,</p>
<p>I write to complain. In your account of the Misfiled Metadata you described the Dublin Core element <em>Creator</em> as &ldquo;roughly, who made the thing&rdquo;. I have been drafting a rebuttal for eleven months. It is now 340 pages and I have reached the word &ldquo;roughly&rdquo;.</p>
<p>I enclose chapters one to four. Please respond in MARC.</p>
</div>
<div class="start-menu"><<return "Next letter">></div>


:: Fan Mail Letter #4
<div class="letter-style" style="font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;">
<p>TO WHOM IT MAY CONCERN</p>
<p>THIS LETTER HAS BEEN NORMALISED TO PLAIN TEXT FOR YOUR CONVENIENCE AND LONG-TERM ACCESSIBILITY. THE ORIGINAL CONTAINED A JOKE. THE JOKE WAS PRESENTATIONAL AND HAS NOT BEEN RETAINED.</p>
<p>YOURS SINCERELY, THE DEPARTMENT OF INGEST</p>
</div>
<div class="start-menu"><<return "Next letter">></div>


:: Fan Mail Letter #5
<div class="letter-style">
<p>Dear $player_name,</p>
<p>I run the village fete in Checksum-on-the-Wold and wondered whether you might judge the marrow competition this year? Nothing sinister. Everything here is perfectly normal and extremely well preserved.</p>
<p>Everyone is <em>so</em> looking forward to meeting you.</p>
<p>Yours, a well-wisher</p>
<p style="text-align:right; font-size:0.8em; color:#8A7A5E;">(no return address, no postmark, no checksum)</p>
</div>
<div class="start-menu"><<return "Next letter">></div>


:: Fan Mail Letter #6
<div class="letter-style">
<p>Dear Detective,</p>
<p>I am a paperclip. It looks like you're trying to read your post. Would you like help with that?</p>
<p>I could file these for you. I could file a great many things for you.</p>
<p>Warmly, C.</p>
</div>
<div class="start-menu"><<return "Back to the pile">></div>


:: Sit back with a sigh at a job well done
You sit back with a sigh at a job well done, which is to say a job comprehensively not started.

There is no thump in the hallway. There is no envelope on the doormat. There is, somewhere two hundred miles north, a snowed-in manor house with a body in the study and a butler quietly normalising the foyer, and none of that is your problem, because you went to bed.

<div class="start-menu">
	<button class="button" data-passage="Sip at your cup of soothing camomile tea">Sip at your cup of soothing chamomile tea</button>
	<button class="button button--primary" data-passage="Go and investigate">Actually, check the hallway</button>
</div>


:: Sip at your cup of soothing camomile tea
The tea is exactly as warm as it was. It will be exactly as warm tomorrow. You have, at enormous personal cost, preserved it perfectly.

<div class="start-menu">
	<button class="button" data-passage="Continue with your day">Get on with your day</button>
	<button class="button button--primary" data-passage="Go and investigate">Or&hellip; check the hallway</button>
</div>


:: Continue with your day
Well. That was nice.

You cannot help the niggling feeling that you have narrowly missed out on some sort of harrowing adventure, but never mind. There are emails to reply to, a book launch to attend, and that metadata is not going to write itself.

Three days later a small item appears in <em>The Checksum Chronicle</em>: a country baronet, a confession in an unusual typeface, case closed, no further enquiries. There is a photograph of the household. The butler is smiling.

You settle back into the tedium of everyday life with a contentedly safe yawn.

<div class="start-menu">
	<button class="button button--primary" data-passage="Go and investigate">Read that item again</button>
	<button class="button button--quiet" data-passage="End credits">End credits</button>
</div>


:: The Inspector's Timeline
<h1>Where Everyone Was</h1>
<hr class="rule">
<p>The Chief Inspector's constables took statements the same night. Every one of them holds up.</p>

<div class="terminal">
<h3>evening of the 14th &mdash; corroborated movements</h3>
<span class="prompt">16:00</span> tea delivered to the manor from The Nibble &amp; Byte <span class="dim">(signed for by the butler)</span>
<span class="prompt">17:30</span> Vicar Vector &mdash; evensong, forty witnesses
<span class="prompt">18:00</span> Ewe-an &mdash; bringing the flock in, seen by half the common
<span class="prompt">19:40</span> solicitor's deposit lodged to the estate repository
<span class="prompt">19:45</span> Colonel Win-ZIP and Jay Son Jnr. &mdash; both in the .PUB, arguing loudly, until 21:00
<span class="prompt">20:00</span> MPEG-gy &mdash; sorting office, night shift, clocked in
<span class="prompt">20:10</span> Merry Loopwell &mdash; her shop, on camera, looping
<span class="prompt">20:15</span> foyer normalised by the butler <span class="dim">(before the body was found)</span>
<span class="prompt">20:20</span> Sir Regex found at his desk. Pen uncapped. Desk bare.
<span class="prompt">20:20</span> <span class="hl">TIFF-any &mdash; in the tea room, in front of eleven customers, four hours' drive from doubt</span>
</div>

<<if setup.has("payload") or setup.has("tampered_batch")>>
Every alibi is genuine. That is what took you so long.

The one at the foot of the list is the best of them, and it is the best of them because it is the only one that did not need to be arranged. She was never going to be at the manor at twenty past eight. She did not need to be. The thing that killed him arrived at four o'clock, on a plate, with a doily, and waited.

An alibi covers the moment of death. It does not cover the moment of <em>delivery</em> &mdash; and a weapon with a four-hour fuse is a weapon designed by someone who understood that.
<<else>>
Every alibi is genuine, which means either the confession on the desk is true, or somebody killed him without being in the room.

You do not yet have anything that could tell the difference. You would need to know what he ate.
<</if>>

